<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Dama Korea uses local browser storage and third-party infrastructure while Google advertising remains inactive." noindex={true}>
  <article class="legal-shell article-body legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated: 21 August 2026</p>
    <h2>Current data use</h2><p>Dama Korea does not operate accounts, a newsletter, an email form or separate analytics. The website does not currently load an analytics script.</p>
    <h2>Heritage worksheet storage</h2><p>The planning worksheet stores checkbox states in this browser under local-storage keys beginning with <code>dama-heritage-</code>. This information remains on the device and is not submitted to Dama Korea. Use the worksheet’s reset button to clear its saved states, or remove site data through the browser’s privacy settings.</p>
    <h2>Current AdSense verification</h2><p>The site includes a Google AdSense publisher meta tag and an <code>ads.txt</code> file for ownership and review verification. It does not currently load AdSense JavaScript, request or display Google-served ads, or set advertising cookies through AdSense.</p>
    <h2>If Google advertising is enabled later</h2><p>Before Google advertising is activated, Dama Korea will configure a Google-certified consent management platform where required and update this policy to describe the active processing. Google explains data use on <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="external">sites that use its services</a>, and advertising choices are available through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="external">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
    <h2>Infrastructure and public corrections</h2><p><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="external">Cloudflare</a> hosts, delivers and protects the site and may process request, network and security data under its own policy. The linked <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="external">GitHub</a> issue tracker processes account and public issue data for corrections, replies and status tracking. Local-storage checklist data is handled by the reader’s browser.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2><p>General content corrections can be raised through the <a href="/contact/">public corrections page</a>. That channel is public and should not contain personal information.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
